<section class="text-level-3">
  <h2>Run tests as part of your CI</h2>

  <if-nodepw>
    <div class="fragment">
      <p class="mt-100r">
        When running on a CI/CD pipeline, the <code>CI</code> env variable should be set to <code>true</code>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-row tiny-gap mt-100r fragment">
      <div>
        <p>By default, with the <code>CI</code> variable</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Failing tests are retried twice</li>
          <li>
            An html report is generated in
            <code>&lt;your-project>/playwright-report</code>
            <br>
            It contains a <code>traces.zip</code> file for the the retried tests
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <pre><code class="ts" data-line-numbers="6,8,12">
          // playwright.config.ts
          import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';
      
          export default defineConfig({
            // ...
            retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
            // ...
            reporter: 'html',
            // ...
            use: {
              // ...
              trace: 'on-first-retry',
              // ...
            },
          });
        </code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-row flex-row--center mt-50r fragment">
      <div class="bubble bubble-bottom-left" style="width: 780px;">
        <i class="emo emo-36 emoji-point-right"></i>
        <div class="bubble__text">
          <p class="text-justify-left">
            Export the <code>playwright-report</code> folder to a web server, <br>
            in a folder named from the execution time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify-left mt-25" style="font-size: 90%;">
            Example:<br>
            http://test-reports.internal/my-product/playwright-2026-06-12_15-30-00<br />
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </if-nodepw>

  <if-pypw>

    Define your CI pytest config in <code>pytest.ci.ini</code>

    <div class="flex-row mt-50">
      <pre style="width: auto;"><code class="ini">
        [pytest]
        addopts = 
            --browser chromium
            --reruns 2
            --numprocesses 3
            --tracing retain-on-failure
            --alluredir allure-results
        env_files_skip_if_set = true
        env_files = 
          .env
      </code></pre>
      <div style="font-size:55%">
        <p><code>--browser</code></p>
        <p class="indented">The browser (<code>chromium</code>, <code>firefox</code>, or <code>webkit</code>), it can be
          specified multiple times.<br>
          <span>https://playwright.dev/python/docs/test-runners</span>
        </p>
        <p><code>--reruns</code></p>
        <p class="indented">Maximum number of times you'd like the failing tests to run<br>
          <span>https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest-rerunfailures</span>
        </p>
        <p><code>--numprocesses</code></p>
        <p class="indented">Run the tests on multiple CPU<br>
          <span>https://pytest-xdist.readthedocs.io/en/latest/distribution.html</span>
        </p>
        <p><code>--tracing</code></p>
        <p class="indented">Whether to record a trace for each test<br>
          <span>https://playwright.dev/python/docs/test-runners</span>
        </p>
        <p><code>--allure</code></p>
        <p class="indented">Path for the test results directory<br>
          <span>https://allurereport.org/docs/pytest/</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>And use it instead of the the default <code>pytest.ini</code></p>

    <pre class="mt-50r"><code class="sh">
      uv run pytest -c pytest.ci.ini
    </code></pre>



  </if-pypw>


</section>

<section>
  <h2>Inspect traces</h2>
  <p class="mt-200r">
    When a tests fails on CI, the console output is offten insufficiant to fix
    the issue
  </p>
  <p class="mt-200r"><strong>Trace files</strong> give much more information</p>

  <div class="mt-200r fragment">
    <p>Inspect traces with</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>npx playwright show-trace path/to/trace.zip</code>
      </li>
      <li class="fragment">
        Or with the online trace viewer:
        <span>https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>